<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nizam Ali Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1734">1734</a>–<a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Asaf Jah II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nizam Ali Khan, Asaf Jah II, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a> from 1762 to 1803 and son of the dynasty's founder. He moved the capital from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangabad">Aurangabad</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a> in 1763. Facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>, he allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and in 1798 accepted a subsidiary alliance, making Hyderabad the leading princely state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nizam-ali-khan.jpg" alt="Nizam Ali Khan" width="250" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mir_Nizam_Ali_Khan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
